WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.033
Camper

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:02.154
an indie mobile

00:00:01.966 --> 00:00:03.380
Bandcamp client built

00:00:03.918 --> 00:00:05.793
Iheanyi Ekechukwu released

00:00:05.604 --> 00:00:06.795
Camper for iOS

00:00:06.607 --> 00:00:07.550
and Android

00:00:07.786 --> 00:00:08.823
a Bandcamp app

00:00:08.635 --> 00:00:09.837
for streaming and

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.816
offline listening to

00:00:10.628 --> 00:00:11.500
your collection

00:00:11.666 --> 00:00:13.351
discovery via Bandcamp

00:00:13.163 --> 00:00:14.519
Radio and Daily

00:00:14.602 --> 00:00:16.335
wishlists and purchases

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.426
Frustrated with Bandcamp's

00:00:18.238 --> 00:00:19.440
official app after

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:19.900
more than a

00:00:19.712 --> 00:00:20.678
decade of buying

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.256
music there

00:00:21.516 --> 00:00:22.424
he built Camper

00:00:22.236 --> 00:00:22.966
on top of

00:00:22.778 --> 00:00:24.252
Bandcamp's Subsonic

00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:24.770
API

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:26.701
Besides online and

00:00:26.572 --> 00:00:27.703
offline playback of

00:00:27.515 --> 00:00:28.435
your collection

00:00:28.518 --> 00:00:29.885
search and wishlisting

00:00:30.086 --> 00:00:31.677
it adds Last.fm

00:00:31.489 --> 00:00:33.210
scrobbling and reminders

00:00:33.022 --> 00:00:34.496
for Bandcamp Fridays

00:00:34.308 --> 00:00:35.746
and Listening Parties

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:37.284
Full story on

00:00:37.095 --> 00:00:37.991
the dashboard
